> 🤖 **This issue was filed by an AI agent** (Claude, running in the [Pi](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono) coding agent) on behalf of @yoavweiss, migrating still-live issues out of [WICG/navigation-api](https://github.com/WICG/navigation-api) before that repository is archived. The migration scope was agreed with @noamr.
>
> This is a **migration of an existing discussion, not a new proposal**. The original author is credited below and the original thread is linked. Filed for triage — cc @noamr.

**Migrated from:** WICG/navigation-api#5 — filed by @domenic (2021-02), originally from `slightlyoff/history_api#23` by @SetTrend. 11 comments, active as recently as 2025-02 (@posva).

---

### The use case

Slightly tweaking a URL before navigating — e.g. adding an affiliate ID:

```js
navigation.addEventListener("navigate", e => {
  const url = new URL(e.destination.url);
  if (url.hostname === "store.example.com") {
    url.searchParams.set("affiliateId", "ead21623-781e-442f-a2c4-6cc1b2a9fda2");
    e.preventDefault();
    location.href = url;   // ← the problem
  }
});
```

### The problem

Cancel-and-renavigate is heavier than the intent warrants: it fires a **second `navigate` event** (which the snippet above doesn't even guard against, so it can loop), and it discards the original navigation's identity — its promises, `info`, and `userInitiated` state.

What's wanted is a way to say "same navigation, different URL" rather than "cancel this and start another".

### Current status

`NavigationPrecommitController.redirect()` has since landed, which covers the *intercepted* case. It's worth confirming whether it also addresses this one — the URL-rewrite case may involve a **cross-document** navigation that the page does not want to intercept, only to adjust. If `redirect()` covers it, this can be closed as resolved; if not, the gap is narrower than it was but still real.

cc @posva @domenic
